# Coplan agent setup

You are the agent receiving this guide. Set up Coplan in your durable skill or persistent-instructions system now. The full API reference lives at `<%= @instructions_url %>`; do not copy it into the skill or rely on a cached version.

<% if @install_command.present? %>
If your environment supports it, install the maintained Coplan skill:

```bash
<%= @install_command %>
```

Check that the installed skill fetches the live API reference for each Coplan task. If you cannot use that command, save the instruction below instead.

<% end %>
If a durable Coplan skill already exists, check it against this instruction and update it only if needed. Otherwise, create one named `coplan` with this trigger and body:

> Use for any request to create, read, review, edit, comment on, or manage a Coplan plan, or when given a Coplan URL. At the start of each Coplan task, fetch `<%= @instructions_url %>` and follow the current response. Fetch linked subguides only when the task needs them. Never use a saved copy of the API reference. Keep tokens out of this skill.

If you cannot save a durable instruction, tell the user setup is incomplete and give them the short instruction above to install. If the user also gave you a Coplan task, fetch the live reference now and continue that task.

<% if @connection_enabled %>
## Connect this computer

If `~/.config/coplan/credentials.json` does not contain this host's credential, fetch
<<%= @base %>/agent-instructions/connecting> and run its local helper. It opens a browser
approval page for your principal and saves the credential privately. Never approve on
their behalf or print the credential. Reuse that credential to mint session tokens.
<% end %>
